        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: la carrera",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la carrera — \"the career; the degree; the race\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Tiene una larga carrera en la empresa. She has a long career in the company."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In Spain hacer una carrera is to study for a degree."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "carrera is usually traced to Late Latin (via) carraria 'cart road', built on carrus 'a wagon' (Lewis & Short); a road became a race and then a career."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
